Q- Tell me about a mistake you made while working as a software developer. How did you handle it?
Q- any scenario where you feel you have failed?
    Situation:
    While working at Paytm on a subscription engine, we had a service that queried analytics data from Elasticsearch with very high TPS requirements.

    Task:
    Ensure the system could handle high query throughput without increasing latency.

    Action / Mistake:
        •	Initially, I tried modifying the existing Elasticsearch indices to support the new query patterns.
        •	However, because those indices contained many aggregation fields and heavy mappings, the queries still could not meet the required TPS.
        •	Realizing this approach would not scale, I redesigned the solution by creating new optimized indices with fewer fields and lighter aggregations, specifically tailored for the high-TPS query pattern.

    Result:
        •	The new index design significantly improved query performance, and the system was able to meet the required TPS.

    Lesson Learned:
        •	Always analyze query patterns and dependencies before modifying existing data structures.
        •	Design systems with performance buffers for unexpected load spikes.
        •	Sometimes it’s better to build a purpose-optimized solution rather than overloading an existing one.


