Q- Tell us about a time when you had to make a big decision for a crucial project
Situation:
At Paytm while working on the Merchant Analytics platform, our existing data processing pipeline was struggling with growing transaction volumes and complex analytics queries.

Decision:
We had to decide whether to keep optimizing the current pipeline or redesign the architecture. I proposed moving to Architecture 2.0 using Apache Spark for distributed data processing.

Action:
	•	Analyzed system bottlenecks and data processing delays.
	•	Evaluated distributed processing frameworks and chose Apache Spark for scalable batch processing.
	•	Led the effort to redesign the pipeline and migrate workloads, which took around 3 months.

Result:
	•	Data processing became much faster and more scalable.
	•	The system handled larger datasets efficiently, enabling more complex analytics for merchants.

Why it was important:
This architectural decision significantly improved the scalability and long-term sustainability of the analytics platform.

