Q. How do you ensure data consistency in distributed systems?
How to ensure data consistency in distributed systems (interview-focused):
	•	Use strong consistency mechanisms when required
	•	    Distributed transactions (e.g., two-phase commit) or consensus protocols.
	•	Event-driven architecture with idempotency
	•	    Ensure operations can be safely retried without duplicating results.
	•	Use versioning / optimistic locking
	•	    Prevent concurrent updates from overwriting each other.
	•	Data replication with consensus
	•	    Systems like Apache Kafka or Apache ZooKeeper use leader-based replication to maintain consistency.
	•	Eventual consistency with reconciliation
	•	    Periodic background reconciliation jobs fix inconsistencies.
	•	Proper ordering and deduplication
	•	    Use message offsets, sequence numbers, or unique IDs.

Example:
At Oracle, we ensured consistency in distributed workflows by implementing task reconciliation and idempotent task execution, so retries did not cause duplicate processing.

